A1. How was Adam before he met Eve? ~ ALONE
A6. What weighs a lot with some people? ~ FAT
A9. What are large cupolas? ~ DOMES
A14. What is made from mint? ~ MONEY
A15. What did the cannibals do when the missionaries brought them religion? ~ ATE
A16. What do many slush funds do? ~ ELECT
A17. Name something that never dries up (init.) ~ US
A18. Name a single womanly argument that wins. ~ TEAR
A20. Name a weighty argument used in Chicago ~ LEAD
A22. Name a Southern State (abbr.) ~ LA
A23. When Federal agents look for speakeasies, what do they rarely ever do? ~ SEE
A25. What were the Siamese twins? ~ SIMILAR
A27. What went over the top in 1918? ~ HAT
A28. What are historical periods? ~ ERAS
A30. What does the tailor do to correct his mistakes? ~ REFIT
A31. What is a fixed decree? ~ FATE
A32. What should one-arm drivers learn to do? ~ STEER
A34. When is a husband's word law? ~ NEVER
A36. What does the policeman do about speakeasies? ~ ATTENDS
A38. In what do you find the best of the English? ~ GRAMMAR
A41. What little word spoiled many a romance? ~ NO
A42. What denotes nearness? ~ AT
A43. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ LA
A44. Who spends $5000 and sometimes gets a quarter back? ~ PA
A45. What is painful? ~ TORMENT
A49. What should bring success? ~ ABILITY
A52. What is the eagle's nest? ~ AERIE
A53. How does the old soak go around? ~ LADEN
A54. What do ambitious painters want to be? ~ PAID
A56. What is a mound erected for a memorial? ~ CAIRN
A58. What is always working against the union? ~ SCAB
A61. What would an uneven distribution be? ~ ODD
A62. What does the bootlegger do to the strength of real whiskey? ~ LESSENS
A64. What is synonymous with stir; bustle? ~ ADO
A65. What adverb means in this or that manner? ~ SO
A66. How was Adam before the fall? ~ BARE
A67. What did the asp that killed Cleopatra resemble? ~ ASPS
A69. Name a personal pronoun. ~ US
A70. What did the tide do last June? ~ EBBED
A72. What verb means "to make free?" ~ RID
A74. What precious stones change color? ~ OPALS
A76. Name something steel plants never grow from (plural). ~ SEEDS
A77. Give a well-known pen name. ~ STY
A78. How was the pie that mother made? ~ TASTY

D1. What must a successful comedian do? ~ AMUSE
D2. Who hates gambling? ~ LOSER
D3. Where do detectives keep their hats? ~ ON
D4. What used to be over the heads of the ladies? ~ NET
D5. What can be said to be "good looking?" ~ EYES
D6. What do politicians go fishing for? ~ FARMERS
D7. What denotes "presence?" ~ AT
D8. What would tattling be in Indiana? ~ TELLING
D9. What is an 8-cylinder car? ~ DEAR
D10. What will Jackie Coogan be when he grows up? ~ OLD
D11. Name a personal pronoun. ~ ME
D12. What is an acclamation? ~ ECLAT
D13. What does a king go around in? ~ STATE
D19. Voting scandals are usually—what? ~ AIRED
D21. What is a fat man? ~ EATER
D24. What did Kipling write about? ~ EAST
D26. What is a famous alibi? ~ IF
D27. What do careless motorists do? ~ HARM
D29. How should apartments be in Winter? ~ STEAMED
D31. What hampers the U. S. Males? ~ FEMALES
D33. What would knockers like to do? ~ ENTER
D35. What kind of an excuse is usually good? ~ VALID
D36. What is busy as a bee? ~ ANT
D37. What adverb means "more than sufficiently?" ~ TOO
D39. What kind of scholar makes the grade? ~ APT
D40. What is a good name for a bright boy? ~ RAY
D46. What happens when a speakeasy proprietor tries to save money? ~ RAID
D47. What does Grandma think nice girls should be? ~ NICER
D48. What are little brothers? ~ TEASERS
D49. What adverb means "before or by some specified time?" ~ ALREADY
D50. What is a notice that eventually leads to matrimony? ~ BANNS
D51. What is an ancient Peruvian prince called? ~ INCA
D54. What does a model young lady do? ~ POSES
D55. What is "home, sweet home" in Spanish America? ~ ADOBE
D57. What is "third person singular, present indicative of 'BE?'" ~ IS
D59. What is a twenty-one-year-old man in Scotland? ~ ADULT
D60. What kind of husbands get shot? ~ BOSSY
D62. What does a lass smile for? ~ LADS
D63. What is "any particular place?" ~ SPOT
D66. What place is famous for its springs? ~ BED
D68. What famous watering place rejuvenates puzzles? ~ SPA
D71. What means "to exist?" ~ BE
D73. What would anyone like to have? ~ IT
D75. What means "in like manner?" ~ AS


